        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/1b136664-fc14-4776-9ede-ba94f5b1af8d,1769385256515/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C278%2C5342%2C3004%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='An in memoriam image is shown on a jumbotron.' width='620' height='349' title='MINNEAPOLIS, MINNESOTA - JANUARY 25: A moment of silence is held for Alex Jeffrey Pretti prior to the start of an NBA game between the Golden State Warriors and Minnesota Timberwolves at Target Center on January 25, 2026 in Minneapolis, Minnesota. Pretti was shot and killed by federal agents in Minneapolis on January 24th. NOTE TO USER: User expressly acknowledges and agrees that, by downloading and or using this photograph, User is consenting to the terms and conditions of the Getty Images License Agreement. (Photo by David Berding/Getty Images)'/><p>The National Basketball Players Association voiced support on Sunday for protesters in Minneapolis, rallying against the deadly presence of U.S. federal immigration authorities.</p>",
